CORE
template-trap.sh
--resolve-dynamic-sites --trace
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[shell-dynamic-site\.1\] .* "rm -f "\*: SUCCESS$
^\[shell-unsupported\.1\] .* the parts of the action of trap for the holes of "rm -f "\* are words .*: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The part of the action for its hole comes from an argument, which may have
a blank.
